# XBD 10.2 Output Devices and Terminal Types
# Copyright (c) 2026 Nicholas Martin. All rights reserved.

assertion  XBD.10.2-output-devices-and-terminal-types.001
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap10.html#10.2
anchor     utilities/od.html#OPTIONS/-t
class      required
says       The control characters of the table of <control> names are the
           bytes 1 to 31 and 127 that od -t a names SOH, STX, ETX, EOT,
           ENQ, ACK, BEL, BS, HT, LF, VT, FF, CR, SO, SI, DLE, DC1, DC2,
           DC3, DC4, NAK, SYN, ETB, CAN, EM, SUB, ESC, FS, GS, RS, US and
           DEL, in that order (A to Z, then [ \ ] ^ _ and ?).
test       t/001-control-names.sh

assertion  XBD.10.2-output-devices-and-terminal-types.002
anchor     basedefs/V1_chap10.html#10.2
class      untestable
says       The system documentation lists the terminal types supported and
           the features and utilities each lacks; a feature a terminal lacks
           is reported by a diagnostic or exit status; keyboards that cannot
           send a <control> character have their sequences documented.
reason     The sentences are about documentation and about which terminal types and features an implementation chooses to support; no test can know what the documentation promises or which type lacks which feature.
